  "body": "I'm testing out the LDAP authentication for synapse. I did ldap3 downgrade as suggested in #1643 \r\nHowever I now have a problem creating users from ldap. \r\nUsers are properly looked up in LDAP: `INFO - POST-5- User authenticated against LDAP server: ldap://ldap.example.lan:389` and synapse at first tries to login as a user `WARNING - POST-5- Attempted to login as @tester:matrix.lan but they do not exist`. Then as I understand it should try to create missing user which it tries to do: `POST-5- ldap registration filter: (&(cn=tester)(objectClass=person))`, but it fails with this warning: `POST-5- LDAP registration failed, no result.`\r\n\r\nAm I missing something?\r\n\r\n",
